<title>USA: Placer, Calif., schools seek OK for $90 mln bonds.</title>
<headline>Placer, Calif., schools seek OK for $90 mln bonds.</headline>
<dateline>SACRAMENTO, Calif. 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Placer, Calif., voters will be asked on March 4 to support a $90 million general obligation bond issue for a local school district, according to a published report on Monday.</p>
<p>If approved by voters next month, the proceeds from Measure A would be used to expand the Placer Union High School District to ease overcrowding, the Sacramento Bee reported.</p>
